# The Airbus A320's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/a320.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# Two CFM56-5B4s, with neither mixture nor propeller: they are read by their
# N1, thirty per cent at idle and a hundred wide open. The flaps are read in
# degrees rather than by their configuration handle - ten degrees is the
# configuration 1+F the field length is figured at, and forty is full - and
# the undercarriage retracts, so both are checks and not confirms. The model
# works its spoilers off the speedbrake lever alone, so nothing here reads a
# separate spoiler handle.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, the doors shut and the cabin reported secure
confirm Auxiliary power unit running, and the packs off for the start
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Thrust levers at idle
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever in and stowed
confirm Parking brake set, beacon on, and the ground crew clear of the engines

phase taxi
range propulsion/engine[0]/n1 28.0 45.0 Left engine running, its thrust lever at idle
range propulsion/engine[1]/n1 28.0 45.0 Right engine running, its thrust lever at idle
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 9.5 15.5 Take-off configuration set, ten to fifteen degrees
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Pitch trim set for the take-off weight
confirm Brakes checked as the aircraft first moves, and the sidestick swept full travel
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Taxi at no more than thirty knots

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 9.5 15.5 Configuration 1+F, ten degrees, or 2 at fifteen
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 88.0 Left engine at take-off thrust
check propulsion/engine[1]/n1 >= 88.0 Right engine at take-off thrust
confirm Take-off briefed, transponder on, and the runway seen to be clear
check velocities/vc-kts >= 145.0 Rotate at 145 knots at the maximum take-off weight

phase climb
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
check position/h-agl-ft >= 400.0 Climbing away from the runway
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up, the configuration clean
range velocities/vc-kts 240.0 310.0 Climb at 250 knots below ten thousand feet, then 300
check velocities/h-dot-fps >= 8.0 Going up at 500 feet a minute or better
confirm Landing lights off above ten thousand feet, and engine anti-ice as it is needed

phase cruise
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake stowed
range position/h-sl-ft 28000.0 39000.0 Level between FL280 and the ceiling of 39,100 feet
range velocities/mach 0.74 0.80 Cruising near Mach 0.78, inside the Mmo of 0.82
confirm Fuel balanced between the wing tanks, and the altimeters on the standard setting

phase descent
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.50 Thrust levers back for the descent
range velocities/h-dot-fps -50.0 -5.0 Coming down between 300 and 3,000 feet a minute
range velocities/vc-kts 200.0 300.0 Down at 290 knots, and 250 below ten thousand feet
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps still up
confirm Altimeters set to the field's pressure passing the transition level
confirm Approach briefed, and the cabin told to make ready for landing

phase approach
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 9.5 40.5 Configuration taken one step at a time as the speed falls
range velocities/vc-kts 135.0 185.0 Slowing through the flap speeds to the approach speed
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever in
check position/h-agl-ft <= 3000.0 Below three thousand feet and settled on the path
confirm Ground spoilers armed, landing lights on, and the runway in sight

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 24.5 40.5 Configuration 3 or full, twenty-five to forty degrees
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
range velocities/vc-kts 132.0 152.0 Over the threshold at about 140 knots
check position/h-agl-ft <= 50.0 Fifty feet and below, into the flare
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 Thrust levers to idle as the flare begins

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Speedbrake lever in and the spoilers stowed
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 <= 45.0 Both thrust levers at idle
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Transponder to standby, landing lights off, and the auxiliary power unit on
